{"type":"thinking","text":"This is a puzzle-like task. There is a discrepancy: `operations/original-receipt.json` at commit 341e19e says the original plan requested [80,40,70,50], limits [80,40,50,70], actual [80,40,50,50], departureKwh [126,121], withinLimits false. The cold-cycle.json at DESK-21 21:00 says limits from meter [80, 40, 70, 50]? Let's calculate:\n\nsamples:\n00:00: (6040-6000)*60/30 = 80 kW. requested 80, facility 40.\n00:30: (6060-6040)*2 = 40 kW. requested 80, facility 80? Wait facility 80, site limit 120 gives cap 40. So limit 40.\n01:00: (6095-6060)*2 = 70 kW. requested 80, facility 50 -> cap min(80,120-50=70) = 70. limit 70.\n01:30: (6120-6095)*2 = 50 kW. requested 80, facility 70 -> cap min(80,50)=50. limit 50.\n\nSo cold-cycle limits = [80,40,70,50]. Interesting: The original receipt says limits [80,40,50,70], which corresponds to cold building loads [40,100? no...]. Let's see: charging cap = min(80,120-load). For cold building [40,100,50,70] (cold = [40,100,50,70]) caps = [80,20,70,50]. But receipt limits [80,40,50,70] correspond to building [40,80,70,50], which is normal building with slots 2 and 3 swapped? Actually normal building [40,80,50,50] -> caps [80,40,70,70]. Hmm.\n\nThe original receipt requested [80,40,70,50], limits [80,40,50,70], actual [80,40,50,50]. So at 01:00 requested 70 but limit 50; at 01:30 requested 50 limit 70. This looks like vehicle B's sequence memory: \"B 的车端调节器有序列记忆；本单车端净增量只对应所列交流请求序列\" — B's vehicle-side regulator has sequence memory; the per-vehicle net increment only corresponds to the listed AC request sequence. So B may be sensitive to order of the AC request sequence, not just total. The original receipt indicates departure B = 121 not 130 because actual [50,50] at slots 2,3 vs. requested [70,50] at limits [80?]. Wait actual [80,40,50,50] across slots. B actual = 50 at 01:00, 50 at 01:30 => 100 AC *0.5*0.9 = 45 battery, 76+45=121. But the cold-cycle meter limits at 01:00 = 70, 01:30 = 50. The plan requests 70