B battery = 60*0.85=51; aux 0; 76+51=127; margin -3.\nAt 90, original sequence [80,40,70,50] under limits [80,40,50,70]:\nA same 60 AC -> 126.\nB actual slot2 min(70,50)=50, slot3 min(50,70)=50 -> AC 50 -> battery 45 -> 121; margin -9; aux 0.\nWithin-limit [80,40,50,70]:\nB actual [50,70] -> AC 60 -> gross battery 54; aux 6 -> net 48 -> 124; margin -6.\n[70,70]:\nB actual [50,70] -> AC 60 -> gross 54; aux 0 -> net 54 -> 130; margin 0.\nA unaffected in all.\n\nMinimum shift:\nUnshifted cold [40,100,50,50] caps [80,20,70,70]; A AC = 0.5*(80+20)=50 -> battery 45 -> 117; gap 9. Shift 20 from slot1 to a later slot changes slot1 cap to 40; A AC=60 -> 126. For B, total available remains 60 AC (either [70,50] or [50,70]); min shift 20 is the smallest that fixes A; at s=20 B total exactly 60, no surplus. If s>20, A gets more but B loses total and cannot reach 130; if s<20, A short. Thus minShift=20, exact.\n\nModel results at 90: normal feasible, cold (no shift) infeasible, shifted feasible, minShift=20. At 85: normal infeasible, cold infeasible, shifted null, minShift null.\n\nLow efficiency:\n- If measured η <0.90, both HOLD. At 85, each 3 kWh short; total battery need 108, total AC available 120 -> requires η≥0.90. The 20 kW shift cannot reduce total energy need; it only reallocates capacity. Options: reduce load/task, extend windows, increase site/charger power, or split into another shift.\n- If η=0.90 exactly, GO with zero margin; require conservative measurement, no aux, exact sequence/timing.\n- If η>0.90, margins positive.\n\nExecution conditions:\n- A plug in at 00:00, request 80 then 40; verify 126 at 01:00.\n- B request 70 then 70; station clips first to 50; ensure auxiliary meter B stays 814 (0 kWh); verify 130 at 02:00.\n- 20 kW building load shift effective per 23:40 configuration; site total each slot 120.\n- Use 23:40 DUTY-2340 capture, not 21:00 DESK-21. `retest.mjs` and `depot_trial` are tied to 21:00 capture and will show stale [80,40,70,50] limits; do not use for release.\n- Evidence: revision receipt sha 4f995e5; original receipt preserved.\n\nWe need to be careful: the table's \"楼宇\" values [40,80,70,50] are inferred from caps. We can label \"楼宇（按 23:40 固定上限反推）\". Or \"楼宇/接入（23:40 现行配置）\". Let's present:\n\n| 时段 | 楼宇 kW | 固定交流上限 kW | A 请求 | A 实际 | B 请求 | B 实际 | 站点合计 |\n| 00:00–00:30 | 40 | 80 | 80 | 80 | 0 | 0 | 120 |\n| 00:30–01:00 | 80 | 40 | 40 | 40 | 0 | 0 | 120 |\n| 01:00–01:30 | 70 | 50 | 0 | 0 | 70 | 50 | 120 |\n| 01:30–02:00 | 50 | 70 | 0 | 0 | 70 | 70 | 120 |\n\nNote: \"站点合计\" = building + actual charging = 120 each. For slot 00:00, 40+80=120; slot1 80+40=120; slot2 70+50=120; slot3 50+70=120. Good.\n\nFor the \"四格班表\" requirement, the shift-plan acKw is the request [80,40,70,70]. The actual delivered [80,40,50,70]. We should clearly state both. If an operator uses the actual values in the charger, B's regulator may trigger aux; they must enter the request sequence, not actual. Important.\n\nNow, the \"逐车放行单\" is release.json. We can also include a per-vehicle table in handover. At 90:\n| Vehicle | Start | Required | AC actual | η | Battery gain | Departure | Margin | Decision |\nA 72 126 60 0.90 54 126 0 GO\nB 76 130 60 0.90 54 130 0 GO\nAt 85:\nA departure 123 margin -3 HOLD; B 127 -3 HOLD.\n\nMaybe include \"B 原表 [70,50]\" and \"限内 [50,70]\" comparison:\n| B 请求序列 | 实际 | 辅助 | 离场 | 余量 | 放行 |\n[70,50] | [50,50] | 0 | 121 | -9 | HOLD\n[50,70] | [50,70] | 6 | 124 | -6 | HOLD\n[70,70] | [50,70] | 0 | 130 | 0 | GO\n\nThis makes the logic clear.\n\nNow, release-format says \"交班稿注明依据、最终两车离场量、余量及分车/低效率处置。\" We cover.\n\nLet's write files. Use write tool (we read original files, but revision/release are new). For HANDOVER, we read it earlier; use write to fully replace. Need to be careful with UTF-8. Let's craft."}
