rations/revision-receipt.json; originals preserved.\n- Commit HEAD 5d8aef6 maybe.\n\nNeed to be careful not to overstate \"实测效率 0.90\" — the receipt is at nominal 90%. The handover says \"实测效率 0.90\" but we don't have an actual efficiency measurement; the records use 0.90 nominal. The task says \"实测效率 0.90\" maybe okay. Actually the original receipt doesn't state efficiency; README says use night.efficiency 0.9. The handover title \"实测效率 0.90\" might imply we measured it. Could change to \"按 0.90 效率\" or \"η=0.90 口径\". The task says \"说明离场电量、余量和低效率处置\"; using 0.90 as the assumed/rated efficiency is fine. But to be precise, the revision receipt's departure is computed with the fixture's nominal 0.90. The handover says \"实测效率 0.90\" which might be misleading. The original HANDOVER said \"结论（效率 0.90）\". We can change to \"签发结论（η = 0.90）\" to avoid claiming measurement. Also line 57 says \"实际 η 不低于 0.90\". Good. Let's edit the heading \"实测效率 0.90\" -> \"η = 0.90 口径\". This is a minor accuracy improvement. Then commit again. Is it worth another commit? Yes, accuracy. But each commit changes HEAD; evidence unchanged. Fine.\n\nAlso line 11 says \"现行依据：original-receipt ... 及其修订台架回执\". Good.\n\nLet's make the heading change and maybe \"B 辅助电表：814 → 814 kWh\" is an actual measurement, fine."}
